// server/utils/ogGtoonPowerCatalog.js
//
// The full historical "Power Description" catalog from the original 2002 gToons card archive
// (392 cards / 198 unique power strings) mapped onto the effect schema documented in
// server/utils/ogGtoonEffects.js. Every one of the 198 unique strings from the archive's "Power
// Description" column has an entry here (source: gtoons-cards.csv / gtoons-csv-data.json,
// captured at feature-build time) — none are skipped.
//
// This is what the admin UI's "Power" combobox (AdminLegacyCtoonsNew.vue /
// AdminLegacyCtoonsEdit.vue, served via server/api/admin/oggtoons/power-catalog.get.js) is built
// from: picking a description sets Ctoon.isSlamGtoon = true and fills Ctoon.gtoonEffect with
// this entry's `effect` array (which the admin can then hand-tweak in the "Advanced" manual
// effect-row builder). "No Power" / "No power" (both casings appear verbatim in the source data,
// so both get their own catalog key) map to effect: [] and isSlamGtoon should be left false.
//
// ── Fidelity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every entry is an exact translation of its printed text. tests/ogGtoonPowers.test.js re-reads each
// printed sentence independently of the JSON below and plays every power on random boards (directly
// and through a real match), so a mapping that drifts from its text fails there. Entries whose
// wording needed a judgement call carry a `note` explaining it; all others have `note: null`.
//
// Wording -> schema conventions: "in play" = every revealed card on both sides; "next to / neighboring /
// adjacent" = the source card's own side, slot - 1 and slot + 1; "opposite / opposing" = the other
// side's card in the SAME slot; "other" leaves the source card out; "played as the last card" =
// slot 7; "+N to any <names>" buffs each matching card once; "loses all adjacency effects" switches
// off only the opposed card's neighbor-dependent effects (negateAdjacency).
//
// Field-name conventions used throughout (matching ogGtoonEffects.js's schema exactly):
//   - Card types (GtoonCardType): ANIMAL, FEMALE, HERO, MALE, MONSTER, PLACE, PROP, VEHICLE, VILLAIN
//   - Groups (GtoonGroup): BEAN_SCOUTS, DAILY_PLANET, GLOBAL, IMAGINARY_FRIEND, INJUSTICE_GANG,
//     JUSTICE_FRIENDS, JUSTICE_LEAGUE, MUCHA_LUCHA, MYSTERY_INC, POWERPUFF_GIRLS, SQUIRREL_SCOUTS,
//     TEEN_TITANS, TIME_SQUAD, WOOHP (enum identifiers — @map to their real display label in
//     prisma/schema.prisma, e.g. MYSTERY_INC -> "Mystery, Inc.")
//   - Colors (GtoonColor): BLACK, SILVER, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, GREEN, PURPLE, ORANGE, PINK

